> Why not use the market to promote your moral values? If you rely on the
> government, sooner or later, there's going to be a 51%, or even 42%,


The theory has been promoted of having two classes of laws originate
from the government.  Those which curtail 'illegal acts'.  And those
which attempt to restrain 'undesirable behaviours'.  Illegal acts are
like killing people or stealing.  They would be punished much like
they are now, by throwing people in jail etc.

Undesirable behaviour laws would be applied to today's 'victimless'
crimes, such as drug use, environmental degradation, gas guzzling,
perhaps abortion.  Rather than outlaw these behaviours outright
and throw the practitioners in jail, (since that doesn't seem to
be working anyway,) the government would adopt more gentle (and 
many say more effective means) to combat these behaviours.  Taxes,
education programs, and licensing are examples of ways in which
such behaviours might be curtailed.  This has worked for cigarettes,
as an example.  The 'carbon tax' is one such concept.

