Subject: [#94-11-505] BASICS: Transhumanist principles

Is it possible to be a statist and a transhumanist at the same time?

As far as I can tell from recent threads on environmentalism some people
are perhaps trying hard. But this is not the first time there have been
reason to raise the question. The topics may vary widely but the basic
issue keeps recurring again and again.

What is it that is so hard to grasp about basic property rights and the
principle of non initiation of force? It should be much harder to device
some variant transhumanism without these. I think those who advocate some
"weaker" form of property rights should explain the principles behind them
and how they may promote transhumanist individuals before arguing coercive
solutions in separate cases.

